t a demonstrated alternative superfamily." url="https://doi.org/10.1101/2022.06.09.495471" publication="bioRxiv preprint, version 1" /><outline text="Robbeets et al. (2022): The response revises datasets and approaches while defending the proposed relationship and the triangulation argument." url="https://doi.org/10.1101/2022.10.05.510045" publication="bioRxiv preprint, version 1" /></outline><outline text="Hachijo" node-id="hach1239" source="glottolog"><outline text="Conditional placements"><outline text="According to Glottolog 5.3: Japonic" url="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18840935" node-ref="japo1237" /><outline text="According to Lee &amp; Hasegawa (2011): Clade: Hachijo, Shizuoka" url="https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2011.0518" node-ref="ph:lee_and_hasegawa2011:105" /></outline></outline><outline text="Ryukyuan" node-id="ryuk1243" source="glottolog"><outline text="Southern Ryukyu" node-id="ryuk1244" source="glottolog"><outline text="Macro-Yaeyama" node-id="macr1267" source="glottolog"><outline text="Yonaguni" node-id="yona1241" source="glottolog"><outline text="Conditional placements"><outline text="According to Glottolog 5.3: Macro-Yaeyama" url="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18840935" node-ref="macr1267" /><outline text="According to Lee &amp; Hasegawa (2011): Clade: Hateruma, Ishigaki, Taketomi …" url="https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.2011.0518" node-ref="ph:lee_and_hasegawa2011:4" /></outline></outline><outline text="Yaeyama" node-id="yaey1239" source="glottolog"><outline text="Kabira" node-id="kabi1263" source="glottolog" /><outline text="Kohama" node-id="koha1246" source="glottolog" /><outline text="Sonai" node-id="sona1243" source="glottolog" /><outline text="Shiraho" node-id="shir1262" source="glottolog" /><outline text="Ishigaki" node-id="ishi1240" source="glottolog"><outline text="Conditional placements"><outline text="According to Glottolog 5.3: Yaeyama" url="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18840935" node-ref="yaey1239" /><outline text="According to Lee &